    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0116" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/572: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-15T19:00:00-05:00">November 15, 1933—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Your No. 2, November 14. As you will recall, a proposed draft of trade
                    agreement was handed to the Brazilian Ambassador on <pb facs="0117" n="29"
                        xml:id="pg29"/> October 30. The Brazilian experts are now engaged in
                    studying this draft in consultation with Rio de Janeiro.</p>
                <p>The inter-departmental sub-committee is actively studying possible concessions on
                    Argentine agricultural commodities as requested in the Argentine Ambassador’s
                    memorandum of October 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>]<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d35-f1"/> These studies should be completed within a few days.</p>
                <p>The Colombian negotiations have made rapid progress and in the absence of
                    unforeseen difficulties should result in the signing of a trade agreement within
                    a few days.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d35-f2"/></p>
                <p>We will telegraph further developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
